    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Navigating a roof insurance claim in Utah requires understanding what is covered, how to work with local contractors, and the step-by-step claims process.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What is Covered vs. Not Covered in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Covered: Sudden, accidental storm damage such as heavy hail, high winds, or fallen tree limbs."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Not Covered: Normal wear and tear, cosmetic aging, or a roof that is past its expected lifespan.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step-by-Step Utah Roof Claim Process"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Get an Independent Inspection First: Have a reputable local roofer inspect the roof and document damage with photos before you call your insurance company. Avoid door-to-door \"storm chaser\" contractors who lack a permanent local address .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Mitigate Further Damage: If the roof leaks, make or authorize temporary emergency repairs (like tarping) and keep all receipts.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "File the Claim: Contact your insurance agent to report the damage and request an adjuster evaluation.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Meet the Adjuster: Walk the property with both the insurance adjuster and your chosen roofing contractor so everyone agrees on the scope of the damage.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review the Settlement: The insurance company will issue an itemized statement detailing your Actual Cash Value (ACV) or Replacement Cost Value (RCV), minus your deductible.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              3
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help you next, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of storm or damage happened (hail, wind, leak)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Is your policy ACV (depreciated payout) or RCV (full replacement)?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
